From: Nura rc4 series <rc4@nura.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: report discarded PD RX messages

The PD PHY raises msg-rx-discarded when a message arrives while RX is
disabled or the buffer is still owned by software. The handler ignored it,
which hid why a self-powered dock never completed PD. Log it at debug
level (dynamic debug) so such races are visible.

Nura-Category: usb-pd
Upstream-Status: candidate
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_pdphy.c
@@ -410,6 +410,10 @@
 		tcpm_pd_transmit_complete(pmic_typec_pdphy->tcpm_port,
 					  TCPC_TX_DISCARDED);
 		break;
+	case PMIC_PDPHY_MSG_RX_DISCARD_IRQ:
+		/* A message arrived while RX was disabled or the buffer busy */
+		dev_dbg(dev, "isr: rx message discarded\n");
+		break;
 	}
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
